<title>FINLAND: FINNISH 8-MTH BEVERAGES SALES FALL 0.9.</title>
<headline>FINNISH 8-MTH BEVERAGES SALES FALL 0.9.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sales in Finland of beer, soft drinks and mineral waters fell 0.9 percent year-on-year in January-August to 476.1 million litres, the Federation of the Brewing and Soft Drinks Industry said on Tuesday.  </p>
<p>Beer sales contracted 4.6 percent to 277.6 million litres with breweries' sales to state-owned ALKO falling 13.2 percent, sales to restaurants falling 9.6 percent and sales to retailer outlets falling 1.2 percent, the federation said.</p>
<p>Sales of soft drinks and mineral waters increased, soft drinks by 4.1 percent year-on-year to 174.1 million litres and mineral waters by 11.3 percent to 24.4 million litres.</p>
<p>--Helsinki Newsroom  +358 - 0 - 680 50 245</p>
